      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "What is the slope of the line $4x-2y=15?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the slope of the line if we can express its equation in slope-intercept form. To do this, we solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2y & =15 \\\\ -2y & =-4x+15 \\\\ 2y & =4x-15 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & =\\frac{4x-15}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x}{2}-\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ y & =2x-\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the slope-intercept equation, we can tell that the slope of the line is $m=2.$",
